|> Exercise
    handle=_cosx_plus_sinx_algebraic_upper_bounding_

    Using only algebra, prove that
    $$
    |\cos x + \sin x| \leq \sqrt{2}
    $$
    for all $x \in \rr$, and
    characterize those $x$'s for which the inequality
    holds with equality.

    |> Solution

        !! Since
        !! $$
        !! |z| \leq A
        !! $$
        !! if and only if
        !! $$
        !! z^2 \leq A^2
        !! $$
        !! for an aribtray real number $z$ and a nonnegative
        !! number $A$, 
        Since we can square the two sides of an
        inequality for which both sides are nonnegative,
        we have

        $$
        \begin{aligned}
        & |\cos x + \sin x| \leq \sqrt{2} \\
        \iff & \up{1.5} (\cos x + \sin x)^2 \leq (\sqrt{2})^2 \\
        \iff & \up{1.5} \cos^2 x + 2\cos x\sin x + \sin^2 x \leq 2 \\
        \iff & \up{1.5} 1 + 2\cos x\sin x \leq 2 \\
        \iff & \up{1.5} 2\cos x\sin x \leq 1 \\
        \iff & \up{1.5} \cos x\sin x \leq {1\over 2}
        \end{aligned}
        $$

        |> ImageLeft
            src=images/e5_cosx_plus_sinx_algebraic_upper_bounding_cloud.svg
            offset_y=0.7em

        ...and we know that the last inequality (even,
        the next-to-last inequality) to be true by
        Exercise >>_ab_inequality_relation_to_sine_cosine_.

        This establishes the inequality.

        For the second part of the question
        we can observe
        that the above sequence of 
        if-and-only-ifs
        also holds
        if we replace “$\leq$” with “$=$” throughout, 
        so equality occurs if and only if

        !! For the second part of the question, 
        !! which is
        !! to characterize the set of $x$'s for which
        !! the inequality holds with equality, 
        !! we can observe
        !! that the above long sequence of 
        !! if-and-only-ifs
        !! also holds
        !! if we replace “$\leq$” with “$=$” throughout, 
        !! so equality occurs if and only if

        $$
        \cos x\sin x = {1\over 2}
        $$

        which, as covered in Note >>_ab_equality_note_ of Exercise >>_ab_inequality_relation_to_sine_cosine_,
        occurs if and only if $\cos x = \sin x$,
        i.e., iff $x \in \{\eta/2 + 2\eta k: k \in \zz\}$.
        !! if and only if $$x \in \{\eta/2 + 2\eta k: k \in \zz\}.$$
        !! which is characterized as those $x$'s for which
        !! $\cos x = \sin x$, or characterized as the set $\{\eta/2 + 2\eta k: k \in \zz\}$,
        !! in Note >>_ab_equality_note_ of Exercise >>_ab_inequality_relation_to_sine_cosine_.

